#
# Golden fixture builders (WI-0.093). They are long straight-line code that fills one table field per line, so
# the per-function complexity limit (which counts every ternary and loop) says nothing useful here. The schema's
# `byte`/`int8` fields are small signed numbers (QP, reference index, sentinel -1), not characters, so the two
# signed-char checks only produce noise on every assignment.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-signed-char-misuse,
  -cert-str34-c
CheckOptions:
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: 120
